{"name":"Knighthood","hex":"#3c3f52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knighthood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An honour whereby one is made into a knight, and whereafter one is entitled to be called Sir.","The quality of being a knight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knighthood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Knighthood (2020 video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Knighthood is a free-to-play, turn-based strategy game developed by Midoki and currently published by Miniclip, previously Phoenix Games and King, in which the player controls a warrior, fighting through levels to gain armour, weapons and other RPG style loot. Knighthood was globally released on February 26, 2020 and is still currently being updated, and has over 5 million downloads on Google Play as of 2023."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Knighthood_2020_video_game_cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knighthood_(2020_video_game)","wikidata":"Q107487212"},{"title":"Knight","blocks":[{"text":"A knight is a person granted an honorary title of a knighthood by a head of state or representative for service to the monarch, the church, or the country, especially in a military capacity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg/330px-Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight","wikidata":"Q102083"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Bayeux_Tapestry_scene57_Harold_death.jpg/500px-Bayeux_Tapestry_scene57_Harold_death.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Bayeux_Tapestry_scene57_Harold_death.jpg/1280px-Bayeux_Tapestry_scene57_Harold_death.jpg?utm_source=